    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28426" root="عذب" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَذَّبَةٌ</span></b>  [for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَمْرٌ مُعَذَّبَةٌ</span>] <i>Wine mixed</i> [<i>with
water,</i> or <i>with some other thing</i> or <i>things</i>]. (A,
TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">معذب</span> [app. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَذَّب</span>] is applied by
the vulgar to Fresh ripe dates <i>soaked with water.</i>
(TA voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْقُوشٌ</span>.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَوْطٌ مُعَذَّبٌ</span> <i>A whip having
an</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِلَاقَة</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَذَبَة</span>] <i>attached to it.</i> (TA.)

